          "kicker": "Eligibility watch",
          "heading": "Former England lock David Ribbans set to become Springbok-eligible on 27 October",
          "body": "Rassie Erasmus has confirmed his interest in David Ribbans, the former England lock who becomes eligible to represent South Africa on 27 October. Ribbans, born in Somerset West and now at Toulon, completes a three-year stand-down period under World Rugby's amended rules, which allow a player who qualifies through birth, citizenship or ancestry to switch. Erasmus said: \"We are also looking at someone like David Ribbans, not that they must get their hopes up.\" Eligibility does not guarantee a switch, and Ribbans has previously said that changing allegiance would not be right towards England."
