        {
          "kicker": "Travel scare",
          "heading": "Louis Bielle-Biarrey stranded at Bristol Airport before Bordeaux Bègles' Gloucester opener",
          "body": "Bordeaux Bègles had four players held at Bristol Airport ahead of their Investec Champions Cup opener against Gloucester, France winger Louis Bielle-Biarrey among them. Loose forward Romain Gardrat, loosehead Matis Perchaud and Tonga's Toma Taufa were also stranded with a fitness coach, a club source told AFP, because their Electronic Travel Authorisations were linked to renewed passports and no new permits had been obtained. The club contacted the French embassy in London, and the issue was eventually resolved, allowing the players to rejoin their teammates."
        },
