          "kicker": "Fly-half form",
          "heading": "Sam Prendergast scores 14 as Leinster beat Clermont 48-23 in Champions Cup",
          "body": "Sam Prendergast scored 14 points and was named Player of the Match for a second successive game as Leinster came from behind twice to beat Clermont 48-23 in Pool 1 of the Champions Cup. The Ireland fly-half turned a 15-16 half-time deficit into a win, and his best moment came two minutes after half-time, when he burst out of defence and kicked for Jimmy O'Brien on the left touchline. Prendergast had lost the No.10 jersey to Jack Crowley midway through the Six Nations."
