      "edition": "Sunday 18 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Bledisloe result",
          "heading": "All Blacks down Wallabies 43-21 in Sydney for 13th straight win",
          "body": "The All Blacks ran in seven tries to Australia's three on Saturday, beating the Wallabies 43-21 in Sydney for their 13th straight win over their trans-Tasman rivals. It follows a 50-19 win at Eden Park that saw New Zealand retain the Bledisloe Cup for the 24th consecutive year. The result has moved the All Blacks to 92.27 rating points, 0.82 behind the Springboks at the top of the World Rugby rankings."
